{"name":"Storksbill White","hex":"#f2f2e2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"storksbill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of genus Pelargonium.","Any plant of genus Erodium."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storksbill"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Erodium","blocks":[{"text":"Erodium is a genus of flowering plants in the botanical family Geraniaceae. The genus includes about 120 species with a subcosmopolitan distribution, native to Europe, North Africa, Asia, Australia, and more locally in North and South America. They are perennials, annuals, or subshrubs, with five-petalled flowers in shades of white, pink, and purple, that strongly resemble the better-known Geranium (crane's-bills). In English-speaking areas of Europe, the species are known as stork's-bills. In North America they are known as filarees or heron's bill."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Erodium_January_2008-2.jpg/330px-Erodium_January_2008-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erodium"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG/500px-Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG/1280px-Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG/500px-Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Erodium lebelii","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Erodium_glandulosum.jpg/500px-Erodium_glandulosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Erodium_glandulosum.jpg/1280px-Erodium_glandulosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","sr